# Hex bolt with thread
#
# Head at the bottom (prints flat, no supports), shank threaded from the foot
# to the tip.
#
# Three OCCT lessons are baked into this model:
# - The helical tool stays fully buried in an oversized blank: a many-turn
#   helical boolean shatters or silently fails when the tool crosses -- or
#   starts near -- a planar end face. The shank is trimmed out afterwards.
# - The groove profile overhangs the shank surface (lead) instead of exactly
#   touching it. A tool tangent to the surface leaves micron-thin sliver
#   solids in the grooves; overhanging the same flank lines cuts the identical
#   groove with zero debris.
# - Adjacent turns of the tool must not touch each other. The crest is the
#   land left between neighbouring grooves, so a fully sharp crest (land = 0)
#   means the swept tool is tangent to itself turn-to-turn, and with any lead
#   it self-intersects; the later `inter` then silently returns nothing
#   (solids 0, exit 0). ISO truncates the crest to pitch/8 for good reason.
#   The guard is: half-width at the tool's outer edge, hw * (lead + gd) / gd,
#   must stay below pitch / 2 -- which is why `lead` shrinks as `land` does.

pitch = 2
r = 4          # shank radius
shank = 24     # shank length
head_h = 6
hr = 8         # hex head circumradius

land = pitch / 8       # crest flat left between grooves (ISO metric truncation)
hw = (pitch - land) / 2   # groove half-width at the shank surface
gd = hw * 1.7320508    # groove depth for 60-degree flanks: half-width / tan(30)
lead = gd / 8          # tool overhang past the shank surface. Sized against the
                       # guard above: hw * (lead + gd) / gd = 1.125 * hw, which
                       # stays under pitch / 2 as long as land >= pitch / 9.
                       # Keep it well away from zero: OCCT 7.9.3's MakePipeShell
                       # has been seen to flip a thin profile inside-out
                       # (negative sweep volume, diff then removes nothing).
groove = polyline [(lead, -(hw * (1 + lead / gd))),
                   (-gd, 0),
                   (lead, hw * (1 + lead / gd))]

# Blank tall enough that the tool (z = 0 .. 26.7) stays buried at both ends.
blank = cylinder r 38 | translate 0 0 12 | diff (helix pitch 26 r | sweep groove)

# Trim the fully-threaded shank out of the blank and seat it on the head.
shaft = blank
 | inter (cylinder (r + 1) shank | floor | translate 0 0 1)
 | translate 0 0 (head_h - 1)

head = polygon 6 hr
 | extrude head_h
 | faces ">Z" | chamfer 2
 | faces "<Z" | chamfer 2

union [head, shaft]
